{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact fddd5d787b68188de3e12c8c50b5f2b3f02829dd for #19245 under review request #19305, judging selected artifact #19304 (2b5b6a0f).\n\nThe [corrected fixture](cmd/gitseq-mcp/main_test.go@fddd5d787b68188de3e12c8c50b5f2b3f02829dd:2180) prepares a signed successor, imports its Git objects, verifies its complete history and encodes both snapshot answers before the production orientation deadline. Copies originate from the same signed template. The first actual HTTP response performs the checked old-head-to-new-head CAS and returns the first orientation; the second returns the prepared successor. Exact two-call, head, depth and non-degraded assertions preserve the real concurrency proof. Fetching objects leaves the consumer's canonical ref unchanged until that CAS; the consumer never rewinds its ref or checkpoint.\n\nIndependent validation in a clean detached checkout: go test -race -count=1 ./cmd/gitseq-mcp -run '^TestWhoami' passed (17.658s), including fallback, invalid/unbounded answers, stall/redirect, fixed two-second budget and warm signed-depth behavior. go vet ./cmd/gitseq-mcp passed. Two separate overlays failed the named assertion as intended: changing only the actual whoami retry limit from two attempts to one yielded one call with truthful degraded fallback (test1.46s); removing only the fixture's ref movement yielded one call and the old depth-one frontier (test1.37s). Both overlays were external to the checkout; production and candidate bytes remain unchanged. Native full MCP race52.890s is attached to the artifact. Independently checked CI34029409294 and Security34029409192 succeeded for this exact head, including fresh full race, vet/build, UI, reproducibility and clone-build gates.\n\nThe original full-suite4.28s degraded failure remains evidence. Source establishes that signing and snapshot construction occurred inside the old deadline; the retained isolated230ms/25ms handler measurements support sensitivity to contention but do not reconstruct the earlier scheduling delay. This correction moves that avoidable setup out of the measured operation without raising a timeout or accepting fallback as success.\n\nArchitecture: the fixture exercises layer1 ordinary Git storage, layer2 kernel verification, layer6 projections/queries and layer7 MCP. Layer3 Nexus/live runtime, layer4 application host binding and layer5 application profile/interpreter remain unchanged, as do the production contracts of the four exercised layers. No contract change requires an architecture-page amendment. The one-file diff is disjoint from the cancellation change between base1b0692 and current main3b718060.\n\nSecurity: imported history is genuinely signed and audited with VerifyAt; the canonical update checks its expected old head and fails visibly on error. Prepared immutable answers retain real roster/frontier evidence. Existing custody, response bounds, redirects, timeout and verified fallback remain exercised. No live workroom, key custody, authority or production behavior is changed; no unresolved security defect found. This is assigned test correction, not decision-chain adoption.\n\nSimplification: the existing template helper, two encoded answers and one in-handler CAS are the smallest clear separation of setup from the concurrent action. No new production seam, timer workaround or duplicate test framework is needed. The selected artifact is fresh and effective. Requester ratification, exact-head sealed delivery, path succession, push and owned-checkout cleanup remain required.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2b5b6a0fe9c81196d13959f9463229105a63186b","head":"fddd5d787b68188de3e12c8c50b5f2b3f02829dd","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7c5f00c95526cf353c57a71bf2767fcbd920bef9\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7c5f00c95526cf353c57a71bf2767fcbd920bef9","revi